WEBVTT

00:00:04.000 --> 00:00:10.000
Moderator: A customer has an escalated ticket. Show me how you'd bring in the success manager.

00:00:16.000 --> 00:00:26.000
Hannah Cho: Normally I'd message the CSM in chat. Let me see what's here. I see a Share with CSM button on the ticket. That's good, one click.

00:00:40.000 --> 00:00:50.000
Hannah Cho: It created a card on the account. Will the CSM see my notes? I want the full ticket history to go with it, not just a summary.

00:01:04.000 --> 00:01:09.000
Moderator: What do you notice on the account page?

00:01:15.000 --> 00:01:26.000
Hannah Cho: The health score is green but this customer has three open escalations. That doesn't make sense to me. I'd lose trust in the score right there.

00:01:40.000 --> 00:01:48.000
Hannah Cho: I want to see how tickets count in the score. Do escalations push it down? There's no way to see that.

00:02:02.000 --> 00:02:12.000
Hannah Cho: The timeline works well. I can see the account's whole history, including what the CSM wrote. We rarely have that visibility.

00:02:26.000 --> 00:02:31.000
Moderator: What would make your team use this daily?

00:02:37.000 --> 00:02:43.000
Hannah Cho: It has to be where we already work. If it's another tab my agents won't open it.

00:02:57.000 --> 00:03:08.000
Hannah Cho: An early signal would be great. If five tickets from the same account arrive in a week, tell the CSM automatically. We find out too late today.

00:03:22.000 --> 00:03:29.000
Hannah Cho: Right now I flag risk by hand, in the queue and again in chat. I want to flag it once.

